---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const lastUpdated = '2026-08-24';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="What CoreFlow collects on this website, why, and how to control it."
>
  <section class="legal">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="kicker">Legal</span>
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <div class="notice">
        <strong>Review before publishing:</strong> the tools named below (Netlify Forms, Cloudflare
        Web Analytics) are the owner's confirmed choices, but neither is fully wired up yet — the
        analytics beacon token and the live Netlify deployment are both still placeholders (see
        <code>Layout.astro</code> and <code>netlify.toml</code>). Confirm both are actually live
        before treating this policy as accurate.
      </div>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>This site collects information in three ways:</p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Consultation request form</strong> (on the About page), handled by Netlify Forms:
          your name, work email, company name, and whatever you write in the message field. We use
          this only to respond to your request and schedule a consultation — we don't sell it, and
          we don't use it for marketing you didn't ask for.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Free guide email capture</strong> (on the ERP Readiness Checklist page), also via
          Netlify Forms: just your email address. The checklist itself is fully readable and
          printable without giving us anything — this form is only for the optional "send me a
          copy" option. If you use it, we'll send the guide and occasionally email about CoreFlow;
          you can unsubscribe at any time.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Website analytics</strong>, via Cloudflare Web Analytics: aggregate,
          non-identifying usage data (which pages are visited, roughly how, from what general
          region). It's cookie-less and doesn't track you individually across other websites — it
          tells us what's working on this site, nothing more.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What we don't do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>We don't sell or rent your information to third parties.</li>
        <li>We don't collect more than the form above asks for.</li>
        <li>We don't use tracking cookies for advertising.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Consultation request details are kept only as long as needed to respond and, if you become
        a customer, as part of that ongoing relationship. You can ask us to delete your
        information at any time — contact us at the email on our <a href="/about">About page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask what information we hold about you, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete
        it. Contact us and we'll act on it.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>Questions about this policy: see the contact details on our <a href="/about">About page</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .wrap {
    max-width: 760px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 64px 24px 80px;
  }
  .kicker {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 11.5px;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-core);
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: 32px;
    margin-top: 10px;
  }
  .updated {
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    font-size: 13px;
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    margin-top: 6px;
  }
  .notice {
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-flow);
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 16px 18px;
    font-size: 13.5px;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin: 28px 0;
  }
  h2 {
    font-size: 19px;
    margin-top: 36px;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  p,
  li {
    font-size: 15px;
    color: var(--color-text);
    line-height: 1.65;
  }
  ul {
    padding-left: 20px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 8px;
  }
</style>
